    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, there is a way to do this. All special keys are implemented as [buffer local mappings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/41487016b71506769c45afac1aee41a180e57fae/doc/mini-starter.txt#L257). Users can use special [`MiniStarterOpened` even](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/41487016b71506769c45afac1aee41a180e57fae/doc/mini-starter.txt#L262) to delete mappings they don't like inside an autocommand. With something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.starter').setup()\r\nlocal disable_ctrl_np = function()\r\n  vim.keymap.del('n', '<C-n>', { buffer = true })\r\n  vim.keymap.del('n', '<C-p>', { buffer = true })\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniStarterOpened', callback = disable_ctrl_np })\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2024-04-23T10:58:15Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/831#issuecomment-2072004523",
